  "title": "Gold and the U.S. Dollar Paradox: Cyclical Volatility in a Secular Repricing of Monetary Assets",
  "summary": "As confidence in the U.S. dollar-based monetary system gradually erodes and central banks seek to further diversify their reserves, gold stands to benefit from its unique position as a neutral, highly liquid monetary asset. Wong explains why market-driven gold selloffs during periods of stress often reflect liquidity needs rather than weakening fundamentals, supporting the broader long-term bullish case for gold.",
